                <p id="shape-intro" class="mb-2 text-dim">High-performance processor design for artificial intelligence — UCSD ENLACE, summer 2023</p>
                <p class="text-muted">ShapeDetectionAI is a real-time shape classifier I built as a research intern at UC San Diego: a linear SVM that recognizes circles, squares, triangles, and stars from tiny 16×16 images, then runs live from a webcam. The twist is hardware thinking — the learned weights are quantized down to 4-bit integers so the same dot-product decision could map efficiently onto silicon.</p>
